1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,461
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,545 --> 00:00:05,714
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,508 --> 00:00:10,635
- <i>♪ Fix it</i> ♪
- <i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,719 --> 00:00:12,762
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,846 --> 00:00:16,725
♪ <i>One cut, and it's over</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,808 --> 00:00:17,642
[Mongki] <i>Atoy is missing.</i>

7
00:00:17,726 --> 00:00:20,186
[Red] <i>But whoever did it,</i>
<i>I hope they kill Atoy.</i>

8
00:00:20,270 --> 00:00:21,271
Less problems for us.

9
00:00:21,354 --> 00:00:23,189
- [Karla] <i>Hey. Are you okay?</i>
- <i>I have to warn Aunt Audrey.</i>

10
00:00:23,273 --> 00:00:24,232
[Gavin] <i>Daddy's men are here.</i>

11
00:00:24,315 --> 00:00:25,525
PREVIOUSLY

12
00:00:25,608 --> 00:00:27,610
- [Karla] <i>Where?</i>
- Before we escaped,

13
00:00:27,694 --> 00:00:30,071
my dad told me

14
00:00:30,155 --> 00:00:32,449
Janine is not my real child.

15
00:00:32,532 --> 00:00:33,283
Huh?

16
00:00:33,366 --> 00:00:35,535
Ame, let's keep this between us. Please?

17
00:00:35,618 --> 00:00:37,245
I need to talk to Atoy first.

18
00:00:37,328 --> 00:00:39,622
Hasn't Atoy come home yet?

19
00:00:39,706 --> 00:00:43,585
[Siony] <i>There's been</i>
<i>so much violence here.</i>

20
00:00:43,668 --> 00:00:45,003
<i>What if he got caught?</i>

21
00:00:45,086 --> 00:00:46,921
[Olga] <i>He's involved</i>
<i>in a major terrorist group.</i>

22
00:00:47,005 --> 00:00:48,298
<i>Do you think you can fight him?</i>

23
00:00:48,381 --> 00:00:52,093
Don't meddle in Uno and Mercado's plan!

24
00:00:52,177 --> 00:00:53,344
[thumps, then thuds]

25
00:00:53,428 --> 00:00:54,554
[grunts]

26
00:00:55,138 --> 00:00:59,642
[Ibyang] Be good to Ibyang!

27
00:00:59,726 --> 00:01:02,062
- [screams]
- [Ibyang] To everyone!

28
00:01:02,145 --> 00:01:03,605
[in English] Mommy!

29
00:01:03,688 --> 00:01:05,023
[in English] Today is the day you'll die.

30
00:01:05,106 --> 00:01:06,524
[in English] And I'm a man of my word!

31
00:01:08,234 --> 00:01:10,612
[music fades]

32
00:01:16,201 --> 00:01:18,995
Hmm? Audrey, are you sure
you don't need help?

33
00:01:19,079 --> 00:01:20,872
It's already done, see?

34
00:01:22,457 --> 00:01:24,209
Do you really know how to cook?

35
00:01:25,376 --> 00:01:28,379
[in English] You tell me. Mmm.

36
00:01:32,842 --> 00:01:33,676
Hmm.

37
00:01:36,930 --> 00:01:38,014
Hey!

38
00:01:41,351 --> 00:01:42,936
The eggs aren't salty.

39
00:01:43,019 --> 00:01:44,479
And the fried rice…

40
00:01:45,522 --> 00:01:46,606
Delicious!

41
00:01:46,689 --> 00:01:48,316
That's good.

42
00:01:48,399 --> 00:01:50,652
I really do know how to cook.

43
00:01:50,735 --> 00:01:53,113
Especially when I was in the States.

44
00:01:53,613 --> 00:01:58,034
But when I came back here,
I didn't do it much.

45
00:01:58,118 --> 00:02:00,078
[somber music playing]

46
00:02:00,161 --> 00:02:01,955
When Janine arrived…

47
00:02:03,957 --> 00:02:06,000
That's when I really became hands-on.

48
00:02:06,876 --> 00:02:09,879
Because I wanted

49
00:02:09,963 --> 00:02:12,841
to prepare everything she needed myself.

50
00:02:12,924 --> 00:02:14,968
[pensive music playing]

51
00:02:15,051 --> 00:02:17,011
[in English] Because I wanted
to take care of my daughter.

52
00:02:21,266 --> 00:02:23,101
So, what now?

53
00:02:26,104 --> 00:02:28,231
Audrey, you know, I think

54
00:02:29,149 --> 00:02:31,526
you need to tell Janine the truth.

55
00:02:33,194 --> 00:02:34,612
I know that too.

56
00:02:37,740 --> 00:02:40,076
But it's not just me
she recognizes as a parent.

57
00:02:41,661 --> 00:02:43,037
Atoy too.

58
00:02:44,455 --> 00:02:45,290
[Audrey scoffs]

59
00:02:45,373 --> 00:02:46,207
[music fades]

60
00:02:46,291 --> 00:02:47,709
[Audrey] I don't know why

61
00:02:48,251 --> 00:02:50,295
everything had to happen now.

62
00:02:52,171 --> 00:02:54,424
Atoy is already going through so much,

63
00:02:55,675 --> 00:02:57,176
and now we've added to it.

64
00:02:57,886 --> 00:02:59,012
[melodramatic music playing]

65
00:02:59,095 --> 00:03:00,179
Lord, please

66
00:03:01,598 --> 00:03:02,891
let him come home safe.

67
00:03:04,434 --> 00:03:06,728
It's Atoy.

68
00:03:07,478 --> 00:03:08,563
He can handle it.

69
00:03:10,148 --> 00:03:12,734
Let's just pray for him.

70
00:03:14,402 --> 00:03:16,362
Everything will be okay.

71
00:03:17,322 --> 00:03:19,407
Even what's happening with your family.

72
00:03:20,658 --> 00:03:21,618
I hope so.

73
00:03:22,827 --> 00:03:24,370
Especially for Janine.

74
00:03:26,372 --> 00:03:29,500
I'm just worried about
what the child will feel.

75
00:03:31,044 --> 00:03:32,837
[in English] I know she's been
through so much.

76
00:03:33,421 --> 00:03:35,548
I don't want her to think she's alone.

77
00:03:41,679 --> 00:03:43,264
Oh. Come on, let's eat.

78
00:03:43,348 --> 00:03:44,557
Let's not waste what you cooked.

79
00:03:44,641 --> 00:03:49,437
[suave theme music playing]

80
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:51,356
[motorcycle revving]

81
00:03:51,439 --> 00:03:52,315
[sewing machine whirring]

82
00:03:52,398 --> 00:03:54,234
[scratches]

83
00:03:54,317 --> 00:03:55,276
[snipping]

84
00:03:56,861 --> 00:03:57,737
[sewing machine clacking]

85
00:03:59,239 --> 00:03:59,948
[gun cocks]

86
00:04:00,031 --> 00:04:02,033
[gunshots]

87
00:04:02,116 --> 00:04:03,326
[clacking]

88
00:04:03,409 --> 00:04:04,827
[clicking]

89
00:04:04,911 --> 00:04:06,246
[snipping]

90
00:04:07,455 --> 00:04:08,873
[electronic blipping]

91
00:04:13,211 --> 00:04:14,087
[music fades]

92
00:04:14,170 --> 00:04:16,881
[line ringing]

93
00:04:16,965 --> 00:04:19,133
[pensive music playing]

94
00:04:23,638 --> 00:04:24,514
[in English] Sir.

95
00:04:25,473 --> 00:04:27,433
[in English] Sir, I have the keys
to the bait vehicle,

96
00:04:27,517 --> 00:04:28,810
and we'll proceed there.

97
00:04:29,310 --> 00:04:33,606
[in English] I'll be approaching,
maybe in 20 minutes or less.

98
00:04:33,690 --> 00:04:36,484
[Mercado on the phone, in English]
<i>Good. Extraction team is in place</i>

99
00:04:36,567 --> 00:04:38,861
<i>and on standby for immediate deployment.</i>

100
00:04:38,945 --> 00:04:40,029
[in English] Copy, sir.

101
00:04:42,323 --> 00:04:43,199
[phone blips]

102
00:04:46,869 --> 00:04:47,745
[music fades]

103
00:04:48,621 --> 00:04:51,207
Huh? Huh? [chuckles]

104
00:04:51,291 --> 00:04:52,917
Sorry. I changed clothes.

105
00:04:53,001 --> 00:04:54,168
[in English] Changed outfit.

106
00:04:54,252 --> 00:04:55,128
- [Olga] Oh, come on.
- Wow.

107
00:04:55,211 --> 00:04:56,546
Let's go to the truck loader.

108
00:04:57,547 --> 00:04:58,548
- Where is it?
- [Uno scoffs]

109
00:04:58,631 --> 00:05:02,385
It wasn't part of our agreement
that you'd join the main operation, right?

110
00:05:02,468 --> 00:05:04,762
People might see you there, Olga.

111
00:05:05,805 --> 00:05:06,639
[scoffs]

112
00:05:06,723 --> 00:05:07,557
[pensive music playing]

113
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:09,934
[stammers] I'll hide!

114
00:05:10,018 --> 00:05:11,936
I'll lie down in the back, and--

115
00:05:12,020 --> 00:05:14,689
Uno, you need more people!

116
00:05:15,481 --> 00:05:17,108
Here I am!

117
00:05:17,191 --> 00:05:18,985
[Olga] I'm all dressed up!

118
00:05:19,068 --> 00:05:22,030
Okay, I'm ready
for the biggest action role of my life!

119
00:05:22,113 --> 00:05:23,406
- [in English] Okay, let's go!
- [in English] Yes.

120
00:05:23,489 --> 00:05:25,283
- Olga, no--
- Shh!

121
00:05:25,366 --> 00:05:27,076
- No, you really can't!
- Shh!

122
00:05:27,744 --> 00:05:29,662
Don't-- Don't worry.

123
00:05:29,746 --> 00:05:30,747
[in English] Okay?

124
00:05:32,081 --> 00:05:34,667
I underwent gun shooting training, and…

125
00:05:34,751 --> 00:05:36,502
- I know how to fight.
- [in English] Okay.

126
00:05:36,586 --> 00:05:38,796
Huh? Not that you asked,

127
00:05:38,880 --> 00:05:42,175
but I guested as a goon
in <i>Hearts on the Badge</i>.

128
00:05:42,258 --> 00:05:44,594
- Wow.
- And also in <i>Encantadia</i>.

129
00:05:44,677 --> 00:05:48,222
A long time ago,
but I was a soldier there.

130
00:05:48,723 --> 00:05:49,724
[smirks] All right.

131
00:05:49,807 --> 00:05:51,559
But still, no.

132
00:05:52,143 --> 00:05:55,438
You're still not included
because if something happens to you,

133
00:05:55,521 --> 00:05:57,023
I'll be responsible.

134
00:05:57,607 --> 00:05:58,483
Clear?

135
00:05:58,566 --> 00:06:00,109
- But--
- But, please.

136
00:06:00,818 --> 00:06:04,739
This operation has a timeline,
and you're causing delays.

137
00:06:05,698 --> 00:06:07,658
It's really not possible,
and that's an order.

138
00:06:07,742 --> 00:06:12,121
[tense music playing]

139
00:06:12,705 --> 00:06:13,998
I braided my hair.

140
00:06:15,124 --> 00:06:16,167
What a waste of an outfit.

141
00:06:17,001 --> 00:06:18,503
- [music fades]
- [grunts, gasps]

142
00:06:18,586 --> 00:06:20,797
- [pensive music playing]
- [huffs]

143
00:06:23,466 --> 00:06:25,176
‪[Lily sighs]

144
00:06:25,259 --> 00:06:26,719
Atoy. [sighs]

145
00:06:29,263 --> 00:06:30,431
What will you do?

146
00:06:31,057 --> 00:06:33,309
Whatever you're planning,
just do it to me.

147
00:06:33,392 --> 00:06:34,685
[in English] Yes, Atoy.

148
00:06:35,394 --> 00:06:36,479
[in English] You will go first.

149
00:06:37,730 --> 00:06:41,734
[in English] We will save Lily.
She has the code for the laptop, but…

150
00:06:42,568 --> 00:06:44,070
she will watch your death.

151
00:06:46,155 --> 00:06:47,115
[in English] Start recording.

152
00:06:48,741 --> 00:06:49,992
[device blips]

153
00:06:50,076 --> 00:06:52,120
[ominous music playing]

154
00:06:57,416 --> 00:06:58,918
[Atoy, in English] Please don't do this.

155
00:06:59,001 --> 00:07:00,419
[in English] I'm begging you.

156
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:01,796
[in English] Please.

157
00:07:02,797 --> 00:07:04,423
[in English] You're begging me?

158
00:07:05,842 --> 00:07:07,718
[in English] Begging me is over.

159
00:07:11,139 --> 00:07:14,684
[in English] I'm going to execute
both of you in front of the camera

160
00:07:15,309 --> 00:07:17,603
and send it to the armed forces.

161
00:07:17,687 --> 00:07:19,355
[in English] So that they'll know

162
00:07:20,231 --> 00:07:21,858
that I am serious.

163
00:07:21,941 --> 00:07:23,067
[music swells]

164
00:07:23,151 --> 00:07:24,819
[Lily] Have mercy on him, please.

165
00:07:24,902 --> 00:07:26,320
- Samir.
- [in English] Please.

166
00:07:26,404 --> 00:07:27,613
[in English] Yes.

167
00:07:27,697 --> 00:07:29,490
- [in English] Samir, have-- have mercy.
- [Atoy, in English] I'm begging you.

168
00:07:29,574 --> 00:07:32,743
[in English] I will not
have mercy on this man!

169
00:07:33,578 --> 00:07:37,915
[in English] And I will kill
many more men just like you

170
00:07:38,708 --> 00:07:44,297
until I get my laptop back from
the military who took it from me!

171
00:07:45,131 --> 00:07:46,382
Military?

172
00:07:46,466 --> 00:07:47,467
What military?

173
00:07:47,550 --> 00:07:48,634
What are you talking about, military?

174
00:07:48,718 --> 00:07:50,011
[stammers] No…

175
00:07:50,094 --> 00:07:52,346
I have nothing to do with…
with the military, not me!

176
00:07:52,430 --> 00:07:54,682
Not me-- No-- No--

177
00:07:54,765 --> 00:07:58,186
[in English] I don't know why
you keep lying to me,

178
00:07:59,437 --> 00:08:03,816
ex-captain Anthony Padua

179
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:06,986
of the Army Ranger Regiment?

180
00:08:07,487 --> 00:08:10,656
[suspenseful music playing]

181
00:08:21,334 --> 00:08:22,168
‪[music fades]

182
00:08:25,338 --> 00:08:29,050
[sinister music playing]

183
00:08:33,596 --> 00:08:35,932
Boss, let's go through the main entrance!

184
00:08:38,726 --> 00:08:39,894
Are you a new driver?

185
00:08:39,977 --> 00:08:41,354
[Uno] Yes.

186
00:08:41,437 --> 00:08:42,522
Where's your helper?

187
00:08:43,022 --> 00:08:44,440
It's his day off, sir.

188
00:08:44,524 --> 00:08:46,192
It's his birthday, he said.

189
00:08:47,318 --> 00:08:48,152
Who?

190
00:08:48,236 --> 00:08:50,029
It's still Jaymar, sir.

191
00:08:50,112 --> 00:08:51,697
It's still Jaymar.

192
00:08:51,781 --> 00:08:52,949
[guard 2] Ah!

193
00:08:53,032 --> 00:08:54,659
So, it's Jaymar's birthday today.

194
00:08:54,742 --> 00:08:56,035
Why didn't he invite us?

195
00:08:57,662 --> 00:08:58,538
Sorry, sir.

196
00:08:58,621 --> 00:09:01,499
But I need to go into the office now.

197
00:09:01,582 --> 00:09:04,460
I still have many invoices to get signed.

198
00:09:07,213 --> 00:09:08,089
Sorry, sir.

199
00:09:10,049 --> 00:09:11,092
Wait!

200
00:09:11,759 --> 00:09:13,678
It's not Jaymar's birthday today.

201
00:09:14,971 --> 00:09:16,806
[rousing music playing]

202
00:09:22,895 --> 00:09:24,772
- Hey, Emerson!
- Eat!

203
00:09:24,855 --> 00:09:25,856
- Eat!
- Brother, eat!

204
00:09:25,940 --> 00:09:27,191
Guys, eat first!

205
00:09:27,275 --> 00:09:28,609
They said they got tired of my pares.

206
00:09:28,693 --> 00:09:31,904
Good thing Sir Nestor will pay for it.

207
00:09:31,988 --> 00:09:33,281
[teasing]

208
00:09:33,364 --> 00:09:34,198
No problem!

209
00:09:34,282 --> 00:09:35,449
- Go ahead!
- [shrieks]

210
00:09:35,533 --> 00:09:36,617
Eat. It's my treat.

211
00:09:36,701 --> 00:09:38,035
I won last night's ending game.

212
00:09:38,119 --> 00:09:39,745
- [laughing]
- [cheering]

213
00:09:39,829 --> 00:09:40,705
No, no, no. It's okay, it's okay.

214
00:09:40,788 --> 00:09:41,831
Uh, we have somewhere to go.

215
00:09:41,914 --> 00:09:44,250
Wa-- wait. Whe-- Where are you going?

216
00:09:44,333 --> 00:09:45,334
Why do your faces look like that?

217
00:09:45,418 --> 00:09:47,253
Looks like you're heading into a fight.

218
00:09:47,336 --> 00:09:48,713
Seems like it.

219
00:09:49,589 --> 00:09:51,215
We're going to rescue Atoy.

220
00:09:51,924 --> 00:09:54,135
It's time we help Atoy.

221
00:09:54,218 --> 00:09:56,012
Uno went in alone.

222
00:09:56,095 --> 00:09:57,138
[Karla] Exactly.

223
00:09:57,221 --> 00:10:00,433
You were told not to go
because it's dangerous, right?

224
00:10:00,516 --> 00:10:03,060
We should leave that
to the experts, brother.

225
00:10:03,644 --> 00:10:04,645
[Gavin, in English] Karla is right.

226
00:10:04,729 --> 00:10:06,355
What if you end up fighting?

227
00:10:06,439 --> 00:10:07,398
[in English] You're not trained.

228
00:10:07,481 --> 00:10:09,442
And if you die?

229
00:10:09,525 --> 00:10:11,319
Then we'll have a wake
here in our community.

230
00:10:11,402 --> 00:10:12,695
- [in English] True.
- Yes.

231
00:10:12,778 --> 00:10:15,281
And I'm scared of those things, brother.

232
00:10:15,364 --> 00:10:16,782
My debut is coming up.

233
00:10:16,866 --> 00:10:19,160
- What a waste of my 18 roses!
- Mmm.

234
00:10:19,243 --> 00:10:20,286
You guys-- What kind…

235
00:10:20,369 --> 00:10:23,164
What kind of town mates
and friends are you, huh?

236
00:10:23,706 --> 00:10:26,459
Our brother needs help now.

237
00:10:26,542 --> 00:10:28,210
[Paldo] Atoy is family.

238
00:10:28,919 --> 00:10:29,962
What's wrong with you?

239
00:10:30,046 --> 00:10:34,258
If any of you were in danger now,

240
00:10:35,384 --> 00:10:38,387
Atoy wouldn't hesitate
to help you. You know that!

241
00:10:38,471 --> 00:10:40,473
Now he needs help,
and you're chickening out?

242
00:10:40,556 --> 00:10:41,599
If you don't want to, then don't!

243
00:10:41,682 --> 00:10:42,516
Let's go, let's go.

244
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:44,310
- We'll go instead!
- [in English] Wait, wait, wait, wait!

245
00:10:44,393 --> 00:10:47,063
For Brother Atoy, fine. I'm in.

246
00:10:48,272 --> 00:10:49,106
Me too!

247
00:10:49,607 --> 00:10:50,483
You're coming?

248
00:10:51,525 --> 00:10:52,860
[in English] Of course.

249
00:10:52,943 --> 00:10:54,779
[in English] I'm not gonna let you
go there without me.

250
00:10:55,613 --> 00:10:57,490
Hmm. Really?

251
00:10:57,573 --> 00:10:59,116
Now you decide to pair up?!

252
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:01,202
As for me, I'll fight for Brother Atoy.

253
00:11:01,285 --> 00:11:03,371
- [Karla] Oh, Jona, oh.
- Oh, if you're fighting…

254
00:11:03,871 --> 00:11:05,247
I'll join too!

255
00:11:05,331 --> 00:11:07,083
- Oh.
- Mmm-hmm!

256
00:11:07,166 --> 00:11:08,084
I'll join too!

257
00:11:08,167 --> 00:11:09,418
[clears throat]

258
00:11:09,502 --> 00:11:11,170
Um, fine.

259
00:11:11,671 --> 00:11:13,339
I'll just pray for you.

260
00:11:13,422 --> 00:11:14,256
Thank you.

261
00:11:14,340 --> 00:11:15,549
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

262
00:11:15,633 --> 00:11:16,926
[in English] What are we waiting for?!

263
00:11:17,009 --> 00:11:18,094
All right, let's fight!

264
00:11:18,177 --> 00:11:19,678
Charge!

265
00:11:19,762 --> 00:11:21,347
- Charge?
- Let's go!

266
00:11:21,430 --> 00:11:22,264
- All right! Charge!
- [clamoring]

267
00:11:22,348 --> 00:11:23,808
All right, all right!

268
00:11:25,101 --> 00:11:26,435
[music fades]

269
00:11:26,519 --> 00:11:27,395
Hey, wait.

270
00:11:27,478 --> 00:11:28,312
- Wait, wait, wait, wait.
- Where?

271
00:11:28,396 --> 00:11:29,855
- Hold on.
- Do you even know where?

272
00:11:29,939 --> 00:11:32,441
- Here.
- There! All together! Let's go there!

273
00:11:32,525 --> 00:11:34,735
- [clamoring]
- [sneaky music playing]

274
00:11:34,819 --> 00:11:35,903
[Karla] Come with us!

275
00:11:39,365 --> 00:11:40,366
Wait!

276
00:11:41,534 --> 00:11:44,328
Who's paying for this?!

277
00:11:44,995 --> 00:11:46,163
[music fades]

278
00:11:46,247 --> 00:11:47,081
[ominous music playing]

279
00:11:47,164 --> 00:11:48,040
Get out!

280
00:11:49,708 --> 00:11:51,168
[Uno] Ouch, sir.

281
00:11:51,669 --> 00:11:53,254
Here's my ID, sir.

282
00:11:53,754 --> 00:11:55,548
I'm really just a new driver, sir.

283
00:11:55,631 --> 00:11:57,716
That's all he told me.

284
00:11:57,800 --> 00:12:00,553
Put that down, sir.
Don't point the gun at me.

285
00:12:00,636 --> 00:12:01,637
Where's your cell phone? Call him!

286
00:12:01,720 --> 00:12:03,889
That's my problem, sir.

287
00:12:03,973 --> 00:12:06,642
My phone is broken. I can't call him.

288
00:12:06,725 --> 00:12:08,561
Put that down, sir.

289
00:12:08,644 --> 00:12:10,020
You keep making excuses. Walk!

290
00:12:10,104 --> 00:12:11,313
Oh, sir! Wait!

291
00:12:11,397 --> 00:12:12,231
Walk!

292
00:12:12,314 --> 00:12:13,232
Sir!

293
00:12:13,315 --> 00:12:19,905
[grunting and groaning]

294
00:12:22,158 --> 00:12:23,367
[music fades]

295
00:12:23,451 --> 00:12:24,618
[gunshots in the distance]

296
00:12:25,286 --> 00:12:26,245
[in English] Gunshots.

297
00:12:26,996 --> 00:12:28,956
[in English] Let's go. You two, stay here.

298
00:12:33,002 --> 00:12:35,379
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

299
00:12:44,805 --> 00:12:46,056
[music fades]

300
00:12:46,140 --> 00:12:47,892
Bro, I'll take over. You go outside.

301
00:12:48,517 --> 00:12:50,686
[grunting and groaning]

302
00:12:50,769 --> 00:12:52,480
- [grunting]
- [gasps]

303
00:12:54,815 --> 00:12:55,774
[gunshots]

304
00:12:55,858 --> 00:12:57,860
[grunting and groaning]

305
00:13:03,073 --> 00:13:04,742
[groans, gasping]

306
00:13:07,870 --> 00:13:09,288
I told you, Ibyang can be relied on.

307
00:13:09,371 --> 00:13:11,165
[nervous chuckle]

308
00:13:14,835 --> 00:13:16,045
- Ouch--
- Oh, sorry, sorry.

309
00:13:16,128 --> 00:13:18,339
[Lily groans]

310
00:13:18,422 --> 00:13:21,383
[music fades]

311
00:13:21,967 --> 00:13:24,386
[action music playing]

312
00:13:35,856 --> 00:13:39,568
[suspenseful music playing]

313
00:13:46,450 --> 00:13:47,368
[groans]

314
00:13:48,536 --> 00:13:51,622
[gunshots]

315
00:14:10,849 --> 00:14:14,895
[foreboding music playing]

316
00:14:31,120 --> 00:14:32,496
[gunshots]

317
00:14:32,580 --> 00:14:33,581
[grunts]

318
00:14:43,757 --> 00:14:45,718
[in English] Sir, no visual of Padua.

319
00:14:46,427 --> 00:14:47,928
But I'm under heavy attack!

320
00:14:48,679 --> 00:14:50,431
I need immediate backup.

321
00:14:52,600 --> 00:14:55,269
[pensive music playing]

322
00:14:56,020 --> 00:14:57,021
[softly] Let's go.

323
00:15:03,152 --> 00:15:05,112
[panting]

324
00:15:10,910 --> 00:15:12,202
Atoy, what now? Where do we go?

325
00:15:13,329 --> 00:15:14,163
Never mind.

326
00:15:14,747 --> 00:15:16,290
We'll find another way. Let's go.

327
00:15:16,373 --> 00:15:18,042
- [gunshots]
- [shrieks]

328
00:15:18,125 --> 00:15:19,293
[gasping]

329
00:15:19,376 --> 00:15:20,544
[thug] Where are you going?

330
00:15:21,128 --> 00:15:22,504
You think you can escape?

331
00:15:23,422 --> 00:15:24,298
Put your gun down.

332
00:15:24,381 --> 00:15:25,424
Down!

333
00:15:26,008 --> 00:15:27,176
All right, all right, all right.

334
00:15:27,676 --> 00:15:29,053
[rousing music playing]

335
00:15:32,348 --> 00:15:33,349
[grunts]

336
00:15:33,432 --> 00:15:35,893
- [ominous music playing]
- [mutters]

337
00:15:35,976 --> 00:15:37,311
Perfect timing.

338
00:15:40,481 --> 00:15:41,398
[sighs]

339
00:15:45,527 --> 00:15:48,072
[music fades]

340
00:15:48,656 --> 00:15:50,366
All right. Take them!

341
00:15:51,867 --> 00:15:52,993
[rousing music playing]

342
00:15:53,077 --> 00:15:53,911
[groans]

343
00:15:53,994 --> 00:15:54,828
[tense music playing]

344
00:15:54,912 --> 00:15:56,455
[grunting and groaning]

345
00:15:59,291 --> 00:16:04,046
[grunting and groaning]

346
00:16:07,883 --> 00:16:10,511
[grunts and groans]

347
00:16:21,772 --> 00:16:24,525
[tense music playing]

348
00:16:37,162 --> 00:16:38,414
Lily, let's go.

349
00:16:39,123 --> 00:16:41,959
[epic music playing]

350
00:16:45,421 --> 00:16:46,547
[Ibyang] Janine!

351
00:16:46,630 --> 00:16:48,007
- What are you doing?
- Give me that!

352
00:16:48,090 --> 00:16:49,633
Come back here!

353
00:16:49,717 --> 00:16:51,468
I just want to talk to my daddy!

354
00:16:51,552 --> 00:16:55,097
And yesterday you didn't let me talk
to Daddy!

355
00:16:55,180 --> 00:16:57,266
He called my phone!

356
00:16:57,850 --> 00:17:01,937
And Tatoy said it's forbidden to call!

357
00:17:02,021 --> 00:17:02,896
[suspicious music playing]

358
00:17:02,980 --> 00:17:03,814
You're so stubborn!

359
00:17:03,897 --> 00:17:05,691
But he's my daddy!

360
00:17:05,774 --> 00:17:06,942
What's your problem?!

361
00:17:07,026 --> 00:17:08,027
[music fades]

362
00:17:09,194 --> 00:17:11,155
I'm not claiming him!

363
00:17:11,238 --> 00:17:12,740
But if you call him,

364
00:17:12,823 --> 00:17:15,492
the people who took him might find out

365
00:17:15,576 --> 00:17:16,952
he has a cell phone!

366
00:17:17,036 --> 00:17:20,039
You know, think before you act.

367
00:17:20,122 --> 00:17:20,998
- Ah, really?
- [Ame] Psst, psst, psst!

368
00:17:21,081 --> 00:17:23,125
- Really?!
- Oh no! You're fighting again, huh?

369
00:17:23,709 --> 00:17:25,753
- You--
- [groans]

370
00:17:26,295 --> 00:17:28,422
Sorry, Sister Ame! Sorry!

371
00:17:29,423 --> 00:17:30,674
- Sorry.
- Janine, even until now,

372
00:17:30,758 --> 00:17:31,800
you're still mean?!

373
00:17:31,884 --> 00:17:32,801
So, what?!

374
00:17:32,885 --> 00:17:34,887
Don't talk back to me like that, huh!

375
00:17:34,970 --> 00:17:35,971
Apologize to Ibyang!

376
00:17:36,555 --> 00:17:38,724
I won't apologize to her. Bleh!

377
00:17:39,433 --> 00:17:42,227
And why should I listen to a dwarf?!

378
00:17:42,311 --> 00:17:43,353
[Ibyang] Hey, hey, hey, hey.

379
00:17:44,063 --> 00:17:45,981
You, that's wrong!

380
00:17:46,565 --> 00:17:48,776
They're called little persons!

381
00:17:48,859 --> 00:17:51,361
I don't care, and I won't apologize.

382
00:17:51,445 --> 00:17:53,655
You know, this isn't even your house!

383
00:17:53,739 --> 00:17:55,908
So, get out, you outsiders!

384
00:17:56,867 --> 00:17:59,870
You know, you have such a bad attitude!

385
00:18:00,579 --> 00:18:02,164
That's why you're not Atoy's child!

386
00:18:02,247 --> 00:18:05,584
You probably got that attitude
from your real parents!

387
00:18:06,251 --> 00:18:07,419
[Audrey] Ame!

388
00:18:08,462 --> 00:18:09,505
[Ame] Audrey.

389
00:18:09,588 --> 00:18:10,672
[in English] Mommy!

390
00:18:11,799 --> 00:18:12,841
Audrey, I'm sorry.

391
00:18:12,925 --> 00:18:15,010
I didn't mean it.
I was just caught off guard.

392
00:18:16,970 --> 00:18:19,640
Mommy, is what she said true?

393
00:18:19,723 --> 00:18:21,266
I'm not your child?!

394
00:18:21,767 --> 00:18:23,143
You're my mommy, right?!

395
00:18:23,644 --> 00:18:26,355
[music fades]

396
00:18:26,438 --> 00:18:27,981
Mommy, what?

397
00:18:28,565 --> 00:18:30,359
You're my real mommy, right?
Why did she say that?

398
00:18:31,110 --> 00:18:32,694
They're lying!

399
00:18:32,778 --> 00:18:34,238
Make them leave!

400
00:18:34,321 --> 00:18:37,407
Get out of here!
What they're saying isn't true!

401
00:18:37,491 --> 00:18:39,284
[screaming]

402
00:18:39,368 --> 00:18:41,328
- [pensive music playing]
- Janine, stop!

403
00:18:42,329 --> 00:18:43,831
[heavy breathing]

404
00:18:43,914 --> 00:18:47,042
Mommy. Mommy,
why are you siding with them?!

405
00:18:47,126 --> 00:18:48,877
What they're saying isn't true!

406
00:18:48,961 --> 00:18:51,004
So, you should take my side!

407
00:18:51,088 --> 00:18:52,381
[sobbing]

408
00:18:52,965 --> 00:18:54,466
Is what she said true?

409
00:18:54,967 --> 00:18:56,051
I'm not your child?

410
00:18:57,427 --> 00:18:58,262
[sobs]

411
00:18:58,345 --> 00:19:00,139
Janine, let's talk first.

412
00:19:00,722 --> 00:19:02,516
[somber music playing]

413
00:19:02,599 --> 00:19:03,559
[in English] No!

414
00:19:04,143 --> 00:19:05,185
[gasps]

415
00:19:06,436 --> 00:19:08,313
[in English] Audrey, sorry, sorry.

416
00:19:10,858 --> 00:19:11,775
Janine!

417
00:19:19,116 --> 00:19:20,200
Wait.

418
00:19:20,284 --> 00:19:22,077
Hmm, sit down here first.

419
00:19:26,874 --> 00:19:27,708
Are you okay?

420
00:19:28,250 --> 00:19:29,543
Uh, what's going on?

421
00:19:30,043 --> 00:19:32,504
I'm… I'm confused.

422
00:19:33,130 --> 00:19:34,631
Jan…

423
00:19:34,715 --> 00:19:36,967
Janine isn't Aunt Audrey's daughter?

424
00:19:41,513 --> 00:19:42,472
Oh, no.

425
00:19:43,599 --> 00:19:45,851
Poor Janine.

426
00:19:46,351 --> 00:19:48,061
[melodramatic music playing]

427
00:19:48,145 --> 00:19:49,229
Wait.

428
00:19:50,272 --> 00:19:52,107
So that means…

429
00:19:53,108 --> 00:19:56,486
Tatoy isn't her daddy?

430
00:19:59,740 --> 00:20:00,657
Yes.

431
00:20:01,491 --> 00:20:03,535
But don't tell her yet.

432
00:20:04,036 --> 00:20:06,955
Let Atoy and Audrey handle it.

433
00:20:07,039 --> 00:20:09,082
Even if Janine fights with you.

434
00:20:10,626 --> 00:20:12,211
Yes, Sister Ame.

435
00:20:12,711 --> 00:20:15,839
Even if Janine is mean to me.

436
00:20:17,382 --> 00:20:20,427
But who could be their real daughter?

437
00:20:22,179 --> 00:20:24,056
[music swells]

438
00:20:24,139 --> 00:20:25,182
[music fades]

439
00:20:28,227 --> 00:20:31,563
[melancholic music playing]

440
00:20:37,319 --> 00:20:39,363
Janine, my child?

441
00:20:41,114 --> 00:20:43,825
Why are you still calling me your child?

442
00:20:44,368 --> 00:20:46,328
I'm not your real child.

443
00:20:55,796 --> 00:20:57,714
Don't say that.

444
00:20:58,924 --> 00:21:00,759
But that's the truth.

445
00:21:01,677 --> 00:21:03,345
Why did you lie to me?

446
00:21:06,223 --> 00:21:09,434
Janine, I only found out

447
00:21:09,518 --> 00:21:11,520
before we ran off to come here.

448
00:21:13,355 --> 00:21:15,899
I didn't tell you yet, because…

449
00:21:17,609 --> 00:21:19,236
I wanted to wait for Atoy.

450
00:21:20,904 --> 00:21:23,073
So that's why Daddy doesn't love me,

451
00:21:23,156 --> 00:21:24,950
because I'm not the real child.

452
00:21:26,118 --> 00:21:27,452
That's not true.

453
00:21:28,453 --> 00:21:30,622
He loves you, child.

454
00:21:31,999 --> 00:21:33,667
Especially me.

455
00:21:34,334 --> 00:21:36,962
[melodramatic music playing]

456
00:21:37,045 --> 00:21:38,630
I'm so sorry this is happening.

457
00:21:38,714 --> 00:21:41,967
Even I'm confused too.

458
00:21:43,677 --> 00:21:46,138
But my view of you hasn't changed.

459
00:21:48,974 --> 00:21:52,185
All the love I showed you, child…

460
00:21:53,603 --> 00:21:55,230
It was all real.

461
00:21:57,232 --> 00:21:58,567
I love you very much…

462
00:22:01,611 --> 00:22:03,739
and I won't leave you.

463
00:22:06,408 --> 00:22:09,786
I am here to love you

464
00:22:10,537 --> 00:22:12,039
and to take care of you

465
00:22:13,457 --> 00:22:15,208
as my own daughter.

466
00:22:15,792 --> 00:22:18,795
[dramatic music playing]

467
00:22:18,879 --> 00:22:21,214
I'm still your mommy, Janine.

468
00:22:22,841 --> 00:22:24,426
No matter what happens.

469
00:22:26,887 --> 00:22:28,263
[in English] You understand?

470
00:22:44,529 --> 00:22:49,618
[tense music playing]

471
00:23:08,470 --> 00:23:10,013
My saint is effective.

472
00:23:10,097 --> 00:23:10,931
So fast.

473
00:23:11,014 --> 00:23:15,268
[gunshots]

474
00:23:21,358 --> 00:23:22,484
[in English] Let's go! Let's go!

475
00:23:23,026 --> 00:23:24,653
[music fades]

476
00:23:28,073 --> 00:23:29,282
[suspicious music playing]

477
00:23:29,866 --> 00:23:32,202
Sir Alcaraz, are you okay there?

478
00:23:32,285 --> 00:23:33,411
I'm still alive, sir.

479
00:23:33,912 --> 00:23:35,163
[operative 1, in English] Men, move!

480
00:23:38,375 --> 00:23:40,627
[operative 2] Go, go, go! Go! Faster!

481
00:23:40,710 --> 00:23:43,338
[music fades]

482
00:24:04,568 --> 00:24:07,612
[ominous music playing]

483
00:24:24,212 --> 00:24:25,881
[footsteps approaching]

484
00:24:31,261 --> 00:24:32,512
Huh?

485
00:24:32,596 --> 00:24:36,600
[footsteps approaching]

486
00:24:39,394 --> 00:24:40,312
Stay there.

487
00:24:40,395 --> 00:24:42,689
[rousing music playing]

488
00:24:52,365 --> 00:24:56,203
[electronic blipping]

489
00:24:56,286 --> 00:25:00,790
[intense music playing]

490
00:25:02,125 --> 00:25:03,335
[Atoy] <i>She's Lily.</i>

491
00:25:03,418 --> 00:25:04,502
She's the decoder.

492
00:25:04,586 --> 00:25:05,921
We need to secure Lily.

493
00:25:06,004 --> 00:25:07,214
She might be targeted again.

494
00:25:07,297 --> 00:25:08,381
‪UP NEXT

495
00:25:08,465 --> 00:25:10,008
[Olga] Ibyang made that.

496
00:25:10,091 --> 00:25:11,551
She said when I return,

497
00:25:11,635 --> 00:25:12,969
we'll be whole again.

498
00:25:13,053 --> 00:25:15,305
But I don't deserve that.

499
00:25:15,388 --> 00:25:16,431
Why not?

500
00:25:16,514 --> 00:25:18,558
You're Ibyang's real father.

501
00:25:18,642 --> 00:25:19,809
[Martina] <i>What now?</i>

502
00:25:19,893 --> 00:25:21,978
That means he might
already be with Audrey.

503
00:25:22,062 --> 00:25:24,981
Good. Because if we find Atoy,

504
00:25:25,065 --> 00:25:27,817
they'll probably be together in one place.

505
00:25:28,902 --> 00:25:30,487
It'll be easier to erase them
from this world.

506
00:25:30,570 --> 00:25:32,614
[Red] <i>I'll take them all down at once.</i>

507
00:25:33,949 --> 00:25:37,369
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

508
00:25:37,452 --> 00:25:42,916
♪ <i>Like a bubble, like a bubble</i> ♪

509
00:25:42,999 --> 00:25:44,501
[music swells]

510
00:25:44,584 --> 00:25:49,005
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

511
00:25:49,089 --> 00:25:50,924
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

512
00:25:51,007 --> 00:25:52,425
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
